Logic ported from other projects
--------------------------------

packages/home/src/reverse/
  The reverse-engineering tools take their logic from REA (https://github.com/morluto/rea,
  MIT). No REA file was copied; each file carries REA's notice, and
  docs/third-party/rea.md lists what came from where.

Open Dot (composio-community/open-dot) has no licence, so it was read for ideas and
never copied. tools/copyscan checks every source file against it on each run of the
test gate.


Downloaded on first setup, not part of this repository
------------------------------------------------------

`python -m orbs_kit.models` (kit/orbs_kit/models.py) fetches these from their own
publishers, under their own licences, and keeps each only if its SHA-256 matches:

  Kokoro-82M (text to speech), via https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx
  Smart Turn v3.2 (end of turn), https://huggingface.co/pipecat-ai/smart-turn-v3
  Whisper base.en (speech to text), as converted by https://huggingface.co/Systran/faster-whisper-base.en

The voice samples in packages/app/public/voices/ were spoken by Kokoro-82M
(tools/voice_samples.py) and are released with Orbz under the MIT License.
